On Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:11:34 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
>> My recommendation is to keep OpenSMTPD and switch its delivery from
>> LMTP to maildir.
>
> Actually I want to keep LMTP in. I like the model that dovecot is the
> only writer. Plus by going through LMTP, Dovecot learns of new messages
> immediately, instead of via a file system scan.

Agreed, LMTP stays, and so does the rule that Dovecot is the only
program that writes the list. I won't send the maildir delivery
change.

Nothing needs to change for this. "[PATCH v11 00/10]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub" [1], posted for
your question about folder creation, already delivers posts over LMTP.
Its patch 7, "[PATCH v11 07/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Take posts
with OpenSMTPD" [2], is unchanged from v10, and the spec's "only
writer" paragraph stands as written.

For the record, the cost we accept is the one the spec already
states: a post made while Dovecot is stopped waits in OpenSMTPD's
queue and lands when Dovecot is back. Step 11 of the acceptance test
checks exactly that.

v11 is still open for review.

